.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt MAN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm man
.Nd read a manual page
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl aw
.Op Ar SECTION
.Ar MANPAGE Ns Op .SECTION
.Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the BusyBox manual reader.
The Rach2 manual begins with
.Xr rach2 7 .
A section may be given before the page name or as a suffix to it.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Display every matching page.
.It Fl w
Print the locations of matching pages.
.El
.Pp
.Ev COLUMNS
sets the width the pager displays at; the installed pages are preformatted
and are not reformatted to it.
.Pp
The manual sections are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 1
Programs.
.It 2
System calls.
.It 4
Devices.
.It 5
File formats.
.It 7
Overviews.
.It 8
Administration.
.El
.Pp
Pages are preformatted text under
.Pa /usr/share/man/catN/NAME.N ,
rendered on the host by mandoc.
The system has no
.Pa man.conf .
.Nm
searches
.Pa /usr/man
and
.Pa /usr/share/man ,
checking
.Pa catN
before
.Pa manN ;
these are the defaults when
.Ev MANPATH
is unset, and a
.Ev MANPATH
given is searched instead.
.Pp
When standard output is a terminal, the pager is selected from
.Ev MANPAGER ,
then
.Ev PAGER ,
then BusyBox
.Xr less 1 .
This build of less supports searches, marks, line numbers, and a status line.
.Pp
When standard output is not a terminal,
.Nm
uses
.Ql col -b -p -x
instead of the pager.
The system's
.Pa /bin/col
copies its input unchanged because the installed pages have no overstrikes.
Thus
.Ql man NAME > FILE
copies the page byte for byte.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/share/man/catN/NAME.N
.It Pa /usr/share/man/catN/NAME.N
Installed preformatted pages.
.It Pa /bin/col
Filter used when standard output is not a terminal.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status does not reflect the pager's exit status.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl man rach2
.Dl man 2 open
.Dl man bootctl
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr less 1 ,
.Xr rach2 7
.Sh HISTORY
